-- title:
--   The branch ideal (U) in the crossing model is prime
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and assume that the quotient $W / (\pi)$ by the ideal generated by $\pi$ is an integral domain. Write $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ for the ring of formal power series in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$, and let `UVCrossingModel W π` be its quotient by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed in the power series ring through the constant-coefficient map; this is the local model of two branches crossing over $\pi = 0$. The theorem asserts that the principal ideal of `UVCrossingModel W π` generated by the element `U π` of that ring is a prime ideal; in particular it is proper, so `U π` is not a unit and the quotient by it is nonzero.
--
--   The ideal `U π` cuts out one of the two branches of the crossing model, and the assertion is that this branch is irreducible in the scheme-theoretic sense, i.e. a point of the spectrum of the model. It is used in the analysis of the minimal primes of the ideal generated by the product of the two branch elements (`minimalPrimes_span_U_mul_V`) and in the recognition of the crossing model inside a complete local ring with maximal ideal generated by a pair of elements whose product is $\pi$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_isPrime_span_U.lean

